              <TabularMCQ id="insight_to_discipline_mapping">
        mode: checkbox
        cols: Psychology, Sociology, Economics, Political Science, Health Sciences
        rows: If a student feels they need to earn money right away to help their family⸴ they might drop out to get a full-time job[Psychology],Conditions like depression⸴ anxiety⸴ or ADHD can interfere with a student's ability to get good grades and remain engaged in school.[Economics, Sociology],A student's environment may increase their likelihood of dropping out if they live in an area affected by gang activity⸴ neighborhood instability⸴ and limited support systems⸴ as seen in some urban communities.[Economics, Sociology],Lack of school funding means fewer resources and support for students, making historically underserved students more likely to drop out.[Political Science]
          </TabularMCQ>
        </TabularMCQGrader>
      </CapaProblem>
