  <SplitPanel id="cause_mapping_with_first_crosslink">
   <LeftPane>
    <Markdown id="cause_mapping_introduction">
## Mapping Causes of High School Dropout
### Introduction

High school dropout is a complex problem with many causes.
Some of the causes include psychological risks like ADHD,
economic pressures from intensive work, family and peer
influences across rural and urban settings, and inequities
in school funding. A more comprehensive understanding of this
problem requires us to study and understand how these causes
relate to one another.
    </Markdown>
    <Markdown id="first_crosslink_sentence">
Students working long hours are likely to come from families with low assets.
These students are most likely trying to help their families financially.
    </Markdown>
   </LeftPane>
   <RightPane>
     <Use id="cause_mapping_2b" ref="cause_mapping_2" />
   </RightPane>
  </SplitPanel>

